# fd — global ignore file, read automatically from $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/fd/ignore.
# No env var or flag needed to enable it; unlike ripgrep's config this is a
# location fd checks on its own.
#
# Format is .gitignore syntax. .gitignore is still respected on top of this,
# so these lines only matter outside a git repo, or for git isn't tracking
# them anyway.
#
# Applies to every fd invocation, including the `find` alias in .zshrc, the
# FZF_DEFAULT_COMMAND / FZF_ALT_C_COMMAND file pickers, and fzf-tab's cd
# preview. The two fzf commands used to carry their own `--exclude .git`
# flag for this; centralised here so plain `fd`/`find` gets the same
# protection instead of only the fzf-driven pickers.

# git doesn't gitignore its own .git directory, so without this fd walks
# thousands of loose objects and packfiles whenever --hidden is set.
.git/

# High-volume directories that are rarely what you meant, for searches run
# outside a repo (inside one, .gitignore already covers these).
node_modules/
.venv/
target/
